---
layout: base.njk
title: Portraits of Change
instrument: true
description: "Portraits of Change, a mixed reality music recital: twelve portraits around the color wheel, live MIDI from acoustic instruments, Hoag Hall, CSU-Pueblo, 28 November 2021."
---
{#
  Content dictates form. The recital already had a structure -- a program of
  twelve pieces that walks once around the color wheel, played by five
  ensembles, each with its own stage plot -- so this page is that program.
  Everything quoted is verbatim from the 2021/2022 research portfolio (see
  _data/portraits.json), misspellings included: the record is not corrected
  in the act of presenting it.
#}
{% from "video.njk" import video, videoScript %}
{% set P = portraits %}
{% macro rgb(c) %}rgb({{ (c[0]*255) | round }}, {{ (c[1]*255) | round }}, {{ (c[2]*255) | round }}){% endmacro %}
{% macro fig(name, caption, cls="") %}
<figure class="{{ cls }}">
  <a href="/images/portraits/{{ name }}.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/images/portraits/{{ name }}.jpg" alt="{{ caption }}" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)]"></a>
  <figcaption class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2">{{ caption }}</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}
{% macro quote(text, cite="") %}
<blockquote class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-secondary)] pl-5 my-6 text-gray-300">
  <p>“{{ text }}”</p>
  {% if cite %}<cite class="block not-italic text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2">{{ cite }}</cite>{% endif %}
</blockquote>
{% endmacro %}

<article class="py-16">

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <header class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-20">
    <p class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm mb-3">The Stage · 2018–2023</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl tracking-tight uppercase font-bold text-white" style="letter-spacing: 0.08em;">{{ P.performance.title }}</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mt-3">{{ P.performance.subtitle }}</p>
    <p class="text-gray-500 mt-2">{{ P.performance.venue }} · {{ P.performance.date }} · twelve portraits</p>

    {{ quote(P.performance.lede, "From the recital program, 2021") }}

    <div id="recording" class="mt-10">
      {{ video(P.performance.video.id, P.performance.video.title, "aspect-video", "maxresdefault") }}
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2">{{ P.performance.video.title }}.</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#program" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white">The program</a>
      <a href="#setup" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white">The setup</a>
      <a href="#theory" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white">The theory</a>
      <a href="#making" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white">The making</a>
      <a href="#archive" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white">The archive</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <section id="program" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto mb-28 scroll-mt-28">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">The program</h2>
      {{ quote("As the songs progress, the main song color will move around the chromatic color wheel throughout the performance.") }}
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">Each portrait below carries its stage-light color, its running time as the length of its bar, the players, and how each instrument reached the machine. The stage plot beside each ensemble is the one drawn for the hall.</p>

      <dl class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm mb-14">
        {% for k in P.key %}
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-bg-card)] border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-lg p-4">
          <dt class="font-mono text-white mb-1">{{ k.term }}</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-400">{{ k.def }}</dd>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </dl>
    </div>

    {% for e in P.ensembles %}
      {% if e.intermissionBefore %}
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto my-12 flex items-center gap-4 text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">
        <span class="flex-1 border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"></span>
        Intermission · {{ e.intermissionBefore }} min
        <span class="flex-1 border-t border-[var(--color-border)]"></span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-8 mb-14">
        <div class="lg:col-span-3 min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm mb-6">{{ e.name }}</h3>
          <ol class="space-y-10">
            {% for p in e.portraits %}
            <li class="grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-4">
              {# Relative luminance picks the numeral's color: black on yellow, white on blue. #}
              {% set lum = p.rgb[0] * 0.2126 + p.rgb[1] * 0.7152 + p.rgb[2] * 0.0722 %}
              <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold {{ 'text-black' if lum > 0.4 else 'text-white' }}" style="background: {{ rgb(p.rgb) }};" aria-hidden="true">{{ p.n }}</span>
              <div>
                <p class="text-white font-semibold">{{ p.title }}</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">{{ p.composer }}</p>

                <div class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-3">
                  <span class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="block h-2 rounded-full" style="width: {{ p.minutes * 10 }}%; background: {{ rgb(p.rgb) }};"></span></span>
                  <span class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-500 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider whitespace-nowrap">{{ p.hue }} · {{ p.minutes }} min</span>
                </div>

                <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-3">{{ p.players }}</p>
                <p class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                  {% for r in p.rig %}<span class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-300 border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded px-2 py-0.5">{{ r }}</span>{% endfor %}
                </p>

                {% if p.note %}<p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-4 italic">“{{ p.note }}”</p>{% endif %}
                {% if p.rigNote %}<p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3 border-l border-[var(--color-border)] pl-3">{{ p.rigNote }}</p>{% endif %}

                {% if p.videoId and p.videoId == P.performance.video.id %}
                  <p class="mt-4 text-sm"><a href="#recording" class="text-gray-300 underline decoration-gray-600 hover:decoration-white">Recording at the top of this page</a></p>
                {% elif p.videoId %}
                  <div class="mt-5 max-w-xl">{{ video(p.videoId, p.title + ", recital, 28 November 2021") }}</div>
                {% endif %}
              </div>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 min-w-0">
          {{ fig(e.plot, "Stage plot: " + e.name + ". Appendix C.", "lg:sticky lg:top-28") }}
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <section id="setup" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-28 scroll-mt-28">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-8">The setup</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
      {{ fig("plot-hardware", "Portraits of Change, Hoag Hall “beta” hardware setup. Appendix C.") }}
      {{ fig("hoag-hall-stage", "Hoag Hall, CSU-Pueblo. Appendix C.") }}
    </div>

    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">From an instrument to the headset, in the order the signal travels:</p>
    <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm mb-4">
      {% for step in ["Instrument", "Condenser mic", "Sonuus G2M, audio to MIDI", "MidiPlus 8×8 interface", "Unity, via Keijiro Takahashi’s Minis", "VFX Graph", "Valve Index + ZED Mini"] %}
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded px-3 py-1 text-gray-300">{{ step }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}<span class="text-gray-600" aria-hidden="true">→</span>{% endif %}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-10">Alongside it: Vive Trackers and Lighthouse base stations place each tracked instrument in the room, and a Behringer FCB1010 foot controller on its own MIDI channel changes effects and songs from the stage.</p>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
      {{ fig("fig05-trumpet-tracker-mic", "Fig 5. Trumpet which has two data inputs for MIDI and for spatial tracking. The vive tracker keeps track of the instrument’s position relative to the world and the condenser mic is fed to the audio-to-midi conversion hardware.") }}
      {{ fig("fig03-midi-pedalboard", "Fig 3. On-stage MIDI interface for audio-to-midi conversion and the main way the desktop PC receives musical information.") }}
    </div>

    {{ quote("The lag is not an issue, since the lag from the computer software and hardware also have up to 20ms of latency from photon to eye of the AR display and sound naturally travels slower than sight.") }}

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mt-14 mb-6">The headset</h3>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-6">
      {{ fig("fig18-mount-design", "Fig 18. A new mount was designed to make use of the magnets at the front of the headset.") }}
      {{ fig("fig19-mount-printed", "Fig 19. The mount was printed in nylon with Multi Jet Fusion printing technology, from the Colorado Springs company ResinFoundry.") }}
      {{ fig("fig20-beta-headset", "Fig 20. The beta headset. 2021") }}
    </div>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mt-14 mb-4">What the system could hear</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Every instrument in the Unity project is named for its channel, its instrument, and whether it is tracked or environmental.</p>
    {{ quote("This allows organizing the software and hardware to be easy to understand and easy to document.") }}
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">The same legibility records the limits. Acoustic instruments reached the machine through audio-to-MIDI converters, each one note at a time:</p>
    {{ quote("It currently uses four Sonuus G2M MIDI converters") }}
    {{ quote("If multiple inputs are given, the output is an approximation or is a missed note entirely.") }}
    <p class="text-gray-400">So the stage plots show players the system never heard. In the brass quintet — five acoustic instruments, four converters — the trombone has no channel. In Bitches Brew, the drums, the second guitar and the second bass stand on the stage without one. What the audience saw was the music as single-note converters and a few native MIDI instruments could describe it: the band the system was wired to hear.</p>
  </section>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <section id="theory" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-28 scroll-mt-28">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">The theory: 12-Node Theory</h2>
    {{ quote("When all interval vectors are built off of a tonic with any arbitrary color or note, it will reveal a color pattern and intervallic relationships that are present in all 12 permutations. This concept is defined as ‘12-Node Theory’ which combines set theory, music theory, and color theory to find aesthetic or interesting intervallic relationships to build contrast, harmony, and dissonance.") }}

    <ol class="grid grid-cols-6 sm:grid-cols-12 gap-2 my-10" aria-label="The twelve nodes and their RGB values">
      {% for c in P.nodes %}
      <li class="text-center">
        <span class="block aspect-square rounded-full" style="background: rgb({{ c[0] }}, {{ c[1] }}, {{ c[2] }});"></span>
        <span class="block text-white text-sm mt-1">{{ loop.index0 }}</span>
        <span class="block font-mono text-[10px] leading-tight text-gray-500">{{ c[0] }}<br>{{ c[1] }}<br>{{ c[2] }}</span>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
      {{ fig("theory-12-nodes", "Fig 7. Color wheel and chromatic music wheel are combined. The set theory method of denoting numbers 0-11 will be used to understand geometric intervallic relationships") }}
      {{ fig("theory-icv6-tritone", "Fig 17. Tritones, or complimentary colors.") }}
      {{ fig("theory-additive", "Fig 10. Additive primary colors are 4 half steps away from each other") }}
      {{ fig("theory-subtractive", "Fig 11. Subtractive primary colors are at the inverse of additive primary colors.") }}
    </div>
    {{ quote("Tri-tones, being the only equally proportionate vector, shows the exact color opposite of the tonic node.") }}

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mt-14 mb-4">Giant Steps</h3>
    {{ quote("Giant Steps shifts between 3 tonics, and when zeroed, are presented as 0-4-8. This shows a triangular relationship on a chromatic wheel.") }}
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
      {{ fig("theory-giant-steps", "Fig 18. Chord analysis of Giant Steps following the change in tonic by following the 2-5-1 chord structure.") }}
      {{ fig("theory-coltrane-triangle", "Fig 19. Visual representation of the tonic movement on a color/music wheel.") }}
    </div>
    {{ quote("Can using color theory give us ideas on how to improvise?") }}
    {{ quote("This hexatonic relationship constructs one of the two whole-tone scales, which is prominently used in improvisation over Giant Steps.") }}

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mt-14 mb-4">Where the theory stops</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-2">Two sentences in the portfolio set its limits. The first is about where the wheel comes from:</p>
    {{ quote("This is truly an arbitrary cut into the color spectrum, and the only reason RGB was chosen is due to the RGB color model that all virtual devices use to generate light.") }}
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-2">The second is the conclusion:</p>
    {{ quote("In any application of audiovisual experiences, the audience’s emotion is what will ultimately connect what they see and hear with what they experience, and the cultural associations with certain sounds and sights will be much stronger in creating specific moods than purely mathematical or geometric associations.") }}
    <p class="text-gray-400">Read now, they are where the project turns. The geometry is exact, but the wheel is cut the way a display emits light, and what a listener experiences comes from a culture the geometry does not contain. That is the question this work leads to: when a practice is made computable, whose perception does the model encode?</p>
  </section>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <section id="making" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-28 scroll-mt-28">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">The making</h2>
    {{ quote("What started as a recital that focused on past innovations in jazz led to exploring new ways of visualizing music.") }}

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-10">
      {{ fig("fig10-first-image-2019", "Fig 10. First Image of Portraits of Change, combining Mixed Reality technology with music. March, 2019") }}
      {{ fig("fig34-first-color-test-2019", "Fig 34. From an early test vid in 2019, this was the first time the color theory was implemented in musical performance in real-time. Damion Kudel plays this test, with a VR side-by-side with the real world. Jul 2019") }}
      {{ fig("fig35-liv-overlay-2019", "Fig 35. Using Liv software, we demonstrated an AR overlay with our MIDI color system for the first time. Aug 2019") }}
      {{ fig("fig37-green-screen-2020", "Fig 37. A mixed reality scene with a green screen and a new trumpet mic to lessen impact on performance sound. Jan 2020") }}
      {{ fig("fig38-creager-2021", "Fig 38. A test with Greg Creager and a student watching him perform in AR. April 2021") }}
      {{ fig("fig33-ar-occlusion-2021", "Fig 33. This is the view through an AR device of the mixed reality music scene with full occlusion of real/virtual objects. May 2021") }}
    </div>

    <h3 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm mb-4">Versions</h3>
    <ol class="border-l border-[var(--color-border)]">
      {% for v in P.versions %}
        {% set href = collections.post | postUrl(v.post) %}
        <li class="pl-6 py-2 relative">
          <span class="absolute -left-[5px] top-4 w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-gray-600"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-gray-500 text-sm mr-3">{{ v.date }}</span>
          {% if href %}<a href="{{ href }}" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white underline decoration-gray-700 hover:decoration-white">{{ v.label }}</a>{% else %}<span class="text-gray-200">{{ v.label }}</span>{% endif %}
          {% if v.videoId %}<span class="text-gray-600 text-xs ml-2" title="Has video">▶</span>{% endif %}
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <section id="archive" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-28 scroll-mt-28">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">The archive</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">The Unity work survives as three repositories, one per generation, with the third-party SDKs archived beside them rather than committed.</p>
    {{ quote("Only 47 of generation 1’s 762 artifacts survive into generation 2 at all. Forcing them into one git history would invent a lineage that never happened.", "Archive README, 2026") }}
    <ul class="space-y-4 my-8">
      {% for a in P.archive %}
      <li class="bg-[var(--color-bg-card)] border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-lg p-5">
        <p class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4"><span class="font-mono text-white">{{ a.repo }}</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-sm">{{ a.years }} · Unity {{ a.unity }}</span></p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">{{ a.line }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-8">Preserved, not maintained</p>
    <a href="/files/portraits-of-change-research-portfolio-2022.pdf" class="sound-interactive interactive-rainbow inline-block px-6 py-3 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider rounded-lg">Research portfolio · PDF, 64 pages</a>
  </section>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <section id="with" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto scroll-mt-28">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">With</h2>
    {{ quote("To the musicians who performed in the project past and present, thank you for taking a chance to see music differently with me.", "Acknowledgements, recital program") }}
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8 text-sm mt-8">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-xs mb-3">At the recital</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Carol Wilson and Tony Szajowski, piano · Jordan Barney and Jay Martinez, bass · Michael Manzanares, drums · Ivan Acurio, trumpet · Ray Beltran, horn · Tyler Perea, tuba · Richard Platt, trombone · DJ Henson, woodwinds · Connor Thomas, saxophone · Thaddeus Zimmerman, guitar · CSU-Pueblo Jazz Ensemble I</p>
        <h3 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-xs mt-6 mb-3">In the tests</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-300">Damion Kudel · Noah Suazo · Greg Creager</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-xs mb-3">In the software</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Keijiro Takahashi, whose open-source Minis and VFX Graph examples the project is built on · Sean Mansell, who wrote the MIDI scene-switching script</p>
        <h3 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-xs mt-6 mb-3">In support</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Fiscally sponsored by Fractured Atlas, March 2019 – August 2021 · CSU-Pueblo Department of Music</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</article>
{{ videoScript() }}
